  "details": "Tamazight is the native language family of around 27 million people across all North Africa. It is divided into numerous sub-languages (not just dialects) that are hardly mutually intelligible. A few examples are Taqbaylit (Central North of Algeria; 3-4 million), Tashelh'it (South West of Morocco; 4-5 million), Tarifit (North of Morocco; 2 million)...\n\nThe diversity might be an issue, but considering cultural factors (more open culture means much higher odds of a speaker playing VRChat), the one worth taking a look at, in my opinion, is Taqbaylit, as i have met a few people speaking despite me only rarely playing the game. As for the other ones, not yet.\n\nFinally, it might be unnecessary to look at them individually because of the low odds of speakers playing the game, I believe an umbrella term for those languages is worth putting into the game; Amazigh. Berber is more of an outdated term given by foreigners while the other one is the people's self given name.",
